/* DISCOVERY / derivation: a TRANSPORTABILITY regret bound for causal control -- controller trained on a
   source domain P, deployed on a target P' (Bareinboim, "Causal AI", Ch 9: transportability). The
   decision-relevant question: how much regret does a source-optimal controller incur on the target? It
   splits into a TRANSPORTABLE part (if the causal effect is recoverable on the target, regret = 0 no
   matter the distributional distance) and a NON-transportable residual bounded by the Wasserstein-1
   distance W1(P,P') via Kantorovich-Rubinstein duality -- the exact object chc.WassersteinPenalty
   penalises. Maxima is the source of truth. */
display2d : false$

C : xt^2*(rr - b^2)^2 / (rr + b^2)^3$
/* deployment regret of the source-optimal control when the target effect is b_tgt = b_src + db */
b_src : b$
R : C*db^2$
print("deployment regret R = C*(b_tgt - b_src)^2 = C*db^2,  C =", C)$

/* (A) TRANSPORTABLE: if the effect is recoverable on the target (db = 0), regret = 0 for ANY
   distributional distance -- transportability, not closeness, is what kills the regret. */
print("(A) transportable (db=0): R =", subst(db=0, R), "  (zero regret, any W1 distance)")$

/* (B) NON-transportable: the effect shifts Lipschitz in the transport distance, db = Lip*d,
   d = W1(P,P'); then R = C*Lip^2*d^2 -- quadratic in the Wasserstein-1 distance. */
Rnt : subst(db = Lip*d, R)$
print("(B) non-transportable (db = Lip*d): R =", Rnt, " = C*Lip^2*d^2 (quadratic in W1)")$

/* Kantorovich-Rubinstein: W1(P,Q) = sup_{f 1-Lipschitz} |E_P f - E_Q f|, so for a Lip-Lipschitz cost
   the deployment cost gap is <= Lip*W1(P,Q). This is the same W1 that chc.WassersteinPenalty uses:
   worst-case over a W1-ball of radius eps = empirical + eps*Lipschitz (Gao-Kleywegt). */
print("KR duality: |E_P' cost - E_P cost| <= Lip*W1(P,P') ; W-DRO worst-case = empirical + eps*Lip")$

/* (C) W-DRO COVERAGE: a robust controller planned for a W1-ball of radius eps has a worst-case regret
   bound C*Lip^2*eps^2; if the true shift d <= eps, this bound COVERS the realized regret C*Lip^2*d^2. */
bound : C*Lip^2*eps^2$
print("(C) W-DRO regret bound(eps) = C*Lip^2*eps^2 ; covers realized when d <= eps:")$
print("    bound(eps) - R_nontransport =", ratsimp(bound - Rnt), " = C*Lip^2*(eps^2 - d^2) >= 0 for eps>=d")$
print("    factor = C*Lip^2*(eps-d)*(eps+d) >= 0 : the robust radius is a transportability budget")$

/* (D) C*Lip^2*eps^2 is the regret to SECOND order in db, not a bound on it. The exact regret of the
   source control u_s = b_s*xt/(b_s^2 + rr) on a target with effect bt is its cost there less the
   target-optimal one, (u_s*k - bt*xt)^2/k with k = bt^2 + rr. Its slope in bt factors into the
   quadratic that vanishes where the regret does and a cubic, so its largest value over
   |bt - b_s| <= Lip*eps sits at an end of that interval or at a real root of the cubic inside it:
   chc.regret.transportability_regret_certificate's exact_wdro_bound. */
us : bs*xt/(bs^2 + rr)$
cost(bt, u) := (bt*u - xt)^2 + rr*u^2$
exact_regret : cost(bt, us) - cost(bt, bt*xt/(bt^2 + rr))$
print("(D) exact regret - (u_s*k - bt*xt)^2/k =",
      ratsimp(exact_regret - (us*(bt^2 + rr) - bt*xt)^2/(bt^2 + rr)))$
print("    its slope in bt, u_s free:",
      factor(diff((u*(bt^2 + rr) - bt*xt)^2/(bt^2 + rr), bt)))$
print("    its second-order term at bt = bs + db:",
      ratsimp(subst(db = 0, diff(subst(bt = bs + db, exact_regret), db, 2))/2 - subst(b = bs, C)))$
defaults : [bs = 1, rr = 1/2, xt = 1]$
at_eps : float(ev(subst(bt = bs + 3/20, exact_regret), defaults))$
print("    defaults, Lip*eps = 0.15: exact at d = eps", at_eps, "over C*Lip^2*eps^2",
      at_eps/float(ev(subst(b = 1, C)*(3/20)^2, defaults)))$
print("    exact at the other end:", float(ev(subst(bt = bs - 3/20, exact_regret), defaults)))$
